## `spec` fields

These are the top-level fields of the Agent spec, the same as `spec:` in YAML. Nested objects are described in the
server's JSON Schema at `GET /v1/schemas` (also used by the UI builder for validation).

| Field | Type | | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `description` | string | optional |  |
| `provider` | string | optional |  Default: `anthropic`. |
| `model` | string | optional |  Default: `claude-opus-5-5`. |
| `runtime` | string | optional | Agent runtime plugin: tool-loop or cli. Default: `tool-loop`. |
| `instructions` | string | optional | System prompt. Default: ``. |
| `skills` | list of string | optional |  |
| `tools` | list of string | optional | Built-in tools, integration actions ('github.create_pull_request', 'github.*'). |
| `subagents` | list of string | optional | Agents this agent may delegate to. |
| `credentials` | list of string | optional | Integrations whose short-lived credentials are injected into the sandbox env, e.g. 'github' or 'github:github-acme' (integration:connection). |
| `sandbox` | string | optional |  |
| `env` | map | optional | Sandbox env; values may use expressions. |
| `limits` | object | optional |  |
| `provider_config` | map | optional | Model settings (temperature, effort, ...). Endpoints and credentials belong on a Gateway. |
| `runtime_config` | map | optional |  |
| `guard` | object | optional | Optional decision-model screening of tool calls. |

